  "question": "Build a complete, beautiful three.js kinetic sculpture for a developer livestream.\nReturn ONLY a complete HTML document, no Markdown fences and no explanation.\nUse THREE from the provided classic script ./vendor/three.min.js (three.js 0.160.1).\nNo other imports, dependencies, network calls, external assets, logos, people, or eval.\n\nThe artwork: a small luminous cobalt core with three orbiting, tilted metallic rings,\nwarm copper accents, and hundreds of tiny particles that travel in coherent orbital\npaths. It should feel like a physical museum sculpture, not a random particle cloud.\nCreate depth through geometry, perspective, materials, and lighting. Use a dark navy\nbackground. Fill the available 16:9 viewport with a legible, balanced composition.\nAvoid huge white lighting hotspots. Use simple procedural geometry and bounded GPU work.\n\nInclude working native Pause/Resume and Reset view buttons, a speed range slider,\nmouse or pointer drag to orbit the view, responsive resize, and a clear title.\nRespect prefers-reduced-motion by starting paused. Show an explicit readable error\nif WebGL is unavailable. Keep all text at least 16px, with strong contrast and visible\nkeyboard focus. Use requestAnimationFrame, cap pixel ratio at 2, and no shadows or\npostprocessing. Make it run offline when served alongside the provided three.js file.\nDon't assume OrbitControls or any add-ons are available. Include all implementation\ninside this single document. Aim for a polished scene, not a technical wireframe.\nKeep the implementation concise: at most 250 lines and 18,000 characters of HTML.\n",
  "answer": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n  <meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\n  <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\">\n  <title>Cobalt Orbital \u2014 Kinetic Sculpture</title>\n  <style>\n    * { box-sizing: border-box; }\n    html, body { margin: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%; overflow: hidden; }\n    body {\n      background: #070d1d;\n      color: #eaf2ff;\n      font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \"Segoe UI\", sans-serif;\n    }\n    button, input { font: inherit; }\n    button:focus-visible, input:focus-visible {\n      outline: 3px solid #8ed0ff;\n      outline-offset: 4px;\n    }\n    canvas { display: block; width: 100%; height: 100%; touch-action: none; cursor: grab; }\n    canvas.dragging { cursor: grabbing; }\n    .title {\n      position: fixed;\n      z-index: 2;\n      top: 22px;\n      left: 26px;\n      pointer-events: none;\n      text-shadow: 0 2px 14px #070d1d;\n    }\n    h1 { margin: 0; font-size: 22px; font-weight: 650; letter-spacing: .18em; text-transform: uppercase; }\n    .subtitle { margin-top: 7px; color: #adc1df; font-size: 14px; letter-spacing: .08em; line-height: 1.5; }\n    .controls {\n      position: fixed;\n      z-index: 2;\n      bottom: 22px;\n      left: 50%;\n      transform: translateX(-50%);\n      display: flex;\n      align-items: center;\n      justify-content: center;\n      gap: 12px;\n      width: max-content;\n      max-width: calc(100% - 24px);\n      padding: 12px;\n      border: 1px solid #3b5277;\n      border-radius: 14px;\n      background: rgba(10, 19, 38, .94);\n      box-shadow: 0 10px 35px #0006;\n    }\n    button {\n      min-height: 44px;\n      padding: 8px 15px;\n      border: 1px solid #56709a;\n      border-radius: 8px;\n      background: #17253e;\n      color: #eaf2ff;\n      cursor: pointer;\n    }\n    button:hover { background: #223654; }\n    .speed { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 9px; padding: 0 3px; }\n    .speed label { font-size: 14px; color: #cbd9ee; }\n    input[type=range] { width: 130px; min-height: 44px; accent-color: #78b9ff; cursor: pointer; }\n    output { min-width: 42px; font-size: 14px; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; color: #cbd9ee; }\n    .hint {\n      position: fixed;\n      z-index: 2;\n      right: 22px;\n      bottom: 24px;\n      color: #97afd0;\n      font-size: 14px;\n      pointer-events: none;\n    }\n    #error {\n      display: none;\n      position: fixed;\n      z-index: 5;\n      inset: 0;\n      place-items: center;\n      padding: 30px;\n      background: #070d1d;\n      text-align: center;\n      font-size: 18px;\n      line-height: 1.6;\n    }\n    @media (max-width: 760px) {\n      .title { top: 16px; left: 16px; }\n      h1 { font-size: 18px; }\n      .subtitle, .hint { display: none; }\n      .controls { bottom: 12px; gap: 8px; padding: 8px; }\n      button { padding: 8px 10px; }\n      input[type=range] { width: 90px; }\n      .speed label { display: none; }\n    }\n  </style>\n</head>\n<body>\n  <header class=\"title\">\n    <h1>Cobalt Orbital</h1>\n    <div class=\"subtitle\">Kinetic study \u00b7 copper, cobalt &amp; light</div>\n  </header>\n  <div class=\"controls\" role=\"group\" aria-label=\"Sculpture controls\">\n    <button id=\"toggle\" type=\"button\">Pause</button>\n    <button id=\"reset\" type=\"button\">Reset view</button>\n    <div class=\"speed\">\n      <label for=\"speed\">Speed</label>\n      <input id=\"speed\" type=\"range\" min=\"0.15\" max=\"2\" step=\"0.05\" value=\"1\" aria-label=\"Animation speed\">\n      <output id=\"speedValue\" for=\"speed\">1.00\u00d7</output>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"hint\">Drag to orbit \u00b7 Scroll to zoom</div>\n  <div id=\"error\" role=\"alert\"></div>\n\n  <script src=\"./vendor/three.min.js\"></script>\n  <script>\n  (() => {\n    'use strict';\n    const error = document.getElementById('error');\n    if (!window.THREE) {\n      error.style.display = 'grid';\n      error.textContent = 'The 3D engine could not load. Please serve this page alongside vendor/three.min.js.';\n      return;\n    }\n    let renderer;\n    try {\n      renderer = new THREE.WebGLRenderer({ antialias: true, powerPreference: 'high-performance' });\n    } catch (e) {\n      error.style.display = 'grid';\n      error.textContent = 'WebGL is unavailable in this browser. Please enable hardware acceleration or use a WebGL-capable browser.';\n      return;\n    }\n    renderer.setPixelRatio(Math.min(window.devicePixelRatio || 1, 2));\n    renderer.setSize(innerWidth, innerHeight);\n    renderer.setClearColor(0x070d1d);\n    renderer.outputColorSpace = THREE.SRGBColorSpace;\n    renderer.toneMapping = THREE.ACESFilmicToneMapping;\n    renderer.toneMappingExposure = .9;\n    renderer.domElement.setAttribute('aria-label', 'Interactive luminous cobalt kinetic sculpture. Drag to orbit the view.');\n    document.body.prepend(renderer.domElement);\n\n    const scene = new THREE.Scene();\n    const camera = new THREE.PerspectiveCamera(43, innerWidth / innerHeight, .1, 100);\n    const home = { theta: .55, phi: 1.18, radius: 12.8 };\n    let theta = home.theta, phi = home.phi, radius = home.radius;\n    let paused = matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches;\n    let speed = 1, time = 0, last = performance.now();\n\n    scene.add(new THREE.HemisphereLight(0x89a8df, 0x170e12, 1.5));\n    const key = new THREE.DirectionalLight(0xffd1a0, 3.1);\n    key.position.set(5, 7, 6);\n    scene.add(key);\n    const fill = new THREE.DirectionalLight(0x618dff, 2.2);\n    fill.position.set(-6, -1, 3);\n    scene.add(fill);\n    const rim = new THREE.PointLight(0xff884d, 35, 18, 2);\n    rim.position.set(-3, 2, -4);\n    scene.add(rim);\n    const coreLight = new THREE.PointLight(0x165dff, 22, 9, 2);\n    scene.add(coreLight);\n\n    const sculpture = new THREE.Group();\n    sculpture.position.y = -.15;\n    scene.add(sculpture);\n\n    // Layered sphere glow: no postprocessing or bloom passes.\n    function glowMaterial(color, opacity) {\n      return new THREE.ShaderMaterial({\n        transparent: true, depthWrite: false, blending: THREE.AdditiveBlending,\n        uniforms: { tint: { value: new THREE.Color(color) }, alpha: { value: opacity } },\n        vertexShader: 'varying vec3 vN; varying vec3 vV; void main(){ vec4 p=modelViewMatrix*vec4(position,1.); vN=normalize(normalMatrix*normal); vV=normalize(-p.xyz); gl_Position=projectionMatrix*p; }',\n        fragmentShader: 'uniform vec3 tint; uniform float alpha; varying vec3 vN; varying vec3 vV; void main(){ float a=pow(1.-abs(dot(vN,vV)),2.2); gl_FragColor=vec4(tint,a*alpha); }'\n      });\n    }\n    const core = new THREE.Mesh(\n      new THREE.IcosahedronGeometry(.47, 4),\n      new THREE.MeshStandardMaterial({ color: 0x073bba, emissive: 0x074bff, emissiveIntensity: 1.65, metalness: .35, roughness: .2 })\n    );\n    sculpture.add(core);\n    const glow1 = new THREE.Mesh(new THREE.SphereGeometry(.72, 24, 16), glowMaterial(0x126cff, .62));\n    const glow2 = new THREE.Mesh(new THREE.SphereGeometry(1.02, 24, 16), glowMaterial(0x064ddd, .22));\n    sculpture.add(glow1, glow2);\n\n    // A museum plinth and fine concentric inlay ground the floating mechanism.\n    const plinth = new THREE.Mesh(\n      new THREE.CylinderGeometry(2.55, 2.8, .24, 96),\n      new THREE.MeshStandardMaterial({ color: 0x111a2a, metalness: .72, roughness: .38 })\n    );\n    plinth.position.y = -3.1;\n    scene.add(plinth);\n    const inlay = new THREE.Mesh(\n      new THREE.TorusGeometry(2.25, .018, 6, 128),\n      new THREE.MeshBasicMaterial({ color: 0xa46037 })\n    );\n    inlay.rotation.x = Math.PI / 2;\n    inlay.position.y = -2.969;\n    scene.add(inlay);\n\n    const steel = new THREE.MeshStandardMaterial({ color: 0x66788d, metalness: .96, roughness: .24 });\n    const copper = new THREE.MeshStandardMaterial({ color: 0xc37543, metalness: .9, roughness: .25 });\n    const ringData = [\n      { radius: 2.0, tube: .072, tilt: new THREE.Euler(.82, .2, .12), rate: .22 },\n      { radius: 2.65, tube: .085, tilt: new THREE.Euler(-.55, .65, 1.05), rate: -.15 },\n      { radius: 3.32, tube: .067, tilt: new THREE.Euler(.4, -.3, -.72), rate: .11 }\n    ];\n    const rings = [];\n    const dummy = new THREE.Object3D();\n    const particlesPerRing = 150;\n    const particleCount = particlesPerRing * ringData.length;\n    const particleGeo = new THREE.SphereGeometry(.025, 6, 4);\n    const particleMat = new THREE.MeshBasicMaterial({ color: 0xa9ceff });\n    const particles = new THREE.InstancedMesh(particleGeo, particleMat, particleCount);\n    particles.instanceMatrix.setUsage(THREE.DynamicDrawUsage);\n    const copperParticles = new THREE.InstancedMesh(particleGeo, new THREE.MeshBasicMaterial({ color: 0xffa467 }), 90);\n    copperParticles.instanceMatrix.setUsage(THREE.DynamicDrawUsage);\n    scene.add(particles, copperParticles);\n    const paths = [];\n\n    ringData.forEach((d, i) => {\n      const group = new THREE.Group();\n      group.rotation.copy(d.tilt);\n      sculpture.add(group);\n      const mesh = new THREE.Mesh(new THREE.TorusGeometry(d.radius, d.tube, 12, 160), i === 1 ? copper : steel);\n      group.add(mesh);\n      // Copper collars are real geometry attached to each orbital ring.\n      for (let j = 0; j < 6; j++) {\n        const a = j * Math.PI / 3;\n        const collar = new THREE.Mesh(new THREE.CylinderGeometry(d.tube * 1.65, d.tube * 1.65, .22, 10), copper);\n        collar.position.set(Math.cos(a) * d.radius, Math.sin(a) * d.radius, 0);\n        collar.rotation.z = a;\n        group.add(collar);\n      }\n      const normal = new THREE.Vector3(0, 0, 1).applyEuler(d.tilt).normalize();\n      const u = new THREE.Vector3(1, 0, 0).applyEuler(d.tilt);\n      const v = new THREE.Vector3(0, 1, 0).applyEuler(d.tilt);\n      paths.push({ u, v, normal, radius: d.radius + .15, rate: d.rate, group });\n      rings.push({ mesh, group, base: d.tilt.clone(), rate: d.rate });\n    });\n\n    const anchors = Array.from({ length: particleCount }, (_, i) => ({\n      a: i % particlesPerRing / particlesPerRing * Math.PI * 2 + Math.sin(i * 12.73) * .18,\n      lane: Math.sin(i * 4.17) * .085,\n      scale: .65 + (Math.sin(i * 8.9) * .5 + .5) * 1.3\n    }));\n    const copperAnchors = Array.from({ length: 90 }, (_, i) => ({\n      a: i / 90 * Math.PI * 2,\n      lane: Math.sin(i * 7.31) * .13,\n      scale: .7 + (Math.sin(i * 5.7) * .5 + .5)\n    }));\n    const p = new THREE.Vector3();\n\n    function placeInstances(mesh, list, ringIndex, offset, t) {\n      const path = paths[ringIndex];\n      list.forEach((d, i) => {\n        const a = d.a + t * (.34 + ringIndex * .07) + offset;\n        const r = path.radius + d.lane;\n        p.copy(path.u).multiplyScalar(Math.cos(a) * r);\n        p.addScaledVector(path.v, Math.sin(a) * r);\n        p.addScaledVector(path.normal, Math.sin(a * 3 + ringIndex) * .055);\n        p.y -= .15;\n        dummy.position.copy(p);\n        dummy.scale.setScalar(d.scale);\n        dummy.updateMatrix();\n        mesh.setMatrixAt(i, dummy.matrix);\n      });\n      mesh.instanceMatrix.needsUpdate = true;\n    }\n\n    function updateCamera() {\n      camera.position.set(\n        radius * Math.sin(phi) * Math.sin(theta),\n        radius * Math.cos(phi),\n        radius * Math.sin(phi) * Math.cos(theta)\n      );\n      camera.lookAt(0, -.35, 0);\n    }\n    updateCamera();\n\n    const toggle = document.getElementById('toggle');\n    const slider = document.getElementById('speed');\n    const output = document.getElementById('speedValue');\n    function syncPause() { toggle.textContent = paused ? 'Resume' : 'Pause'; }\n    syncPause();\n    toggle.addEventListener('click', () => { paused = !paused; syncPause(); });\n    slider.addEventListener('input', () => {\n      speed = Number(slider.value);\n      output.value = speed.toFixed(2) + '\u00d7';\n    });\n    document.getElementById('reset').addEventListener('click', () => {\n      theta = home.theta; phi = home.phi; radius = home.radius; updateCamera();\n    });\n\n    let dragging = false, lastX = 0, lastY = 0;\n    const canvas = renderer.domElement;\n    canvas.addEventListener('pointerdown', e => {\n      dragging = true; lastX = e.clientX; lastY = e.clientY;\n      canvas.classList.add('dragging'); canvas.setPointerCapture(e.pointerId);\n    });\n    canvas.addEventListener('pointermove', e => {\n      if (!dragging) return;\n      theta -= (e.clientX - lastX) * .006;\n      phi = Math.max(.22, Math.min(Math.PI - .22, phi - (e.clientY - lastY) * .006));\n      lastX = e.clientX; lastY = e.clientY; updateCamera();\n    });\n    function endDrag() { dragging = false; canvas.classList.remove('dragging'); }\n    canvas.addEventListener('pointerup', endDrag);\n    canvas.addEventListener('pointercancel', endDrag);\n    canvas.addEventListener('wheel', e => {\n      e.preventDefault();\n      radius = Math.max(7.5, Math.min(22, radius * Math.exp(e.deltaY * .001)));\n      updateCamera();\n    }, { passive: false });\n\n    addEventListener('resize', () => {\n      camera.aspect = innerWidth / innerHeight;\n      camera.updateProjectionMatrix();\n      renderer.setPixelRatio(Math.min(window.devicePixelRatio || 1, 2));\n      renderer.setSize(innerWidth, innerHeight);\n    });\n    matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').addEventListener('change', e => {\n      if (e.matches) { paused = true; syncPause(); }\n    });\n\n    function frame(now) {\n      requestAnimationFrame(frame);\n      const dt = Math.min((now - last) / 1000, .05);\n      last = now;\n      if (paused) return;\n      time += dt * speed;\n      rings.forEach((r, i) => {\n        r.group.rotation.z = r.base.z + Math.sin(time * .22 + i * 2) * .12;\n        r.group.rotation.y = r.base.y + time * r.rate * .24;\n      });\n      // Recalculate transformed path bases after the rings precess.\n      paths.forEach((path, i) => {\n        const e = rings[i].group.rotation;\n        path.u.set(1, 0, 0).applyEuler(e);\n        path.v.set(0, 1, 0).applyEuler(e);\n        path.normal.set(0, 0, 1).applyEuler(e).normalize();\n      });\n      const pulse = 1 + Math.sin(time * 1.6) * .025;\n      core.scale.setScalar(pulse);\n      glow1.scale.setScalar(1 + Math.sin(time * 1.2) * .06);\n      coreLight.intensity = 20 + Math.sin(time * 1.6) * 3;\n      placeInstances(particles, anchors, 0, 0, time);\n      // Divide the blue instances among all three orbital paths.\n      anchors.forEach((d, i) => {\n        const ri = i % 3, path = paths[ri];\n        const a = d.a + time * (.34 + ri * .07);\n        const r = path.radius + d.lane;\n        p.copy(path.u).multiplyScalar(Math.cos(a) * r).addScaledVector(path.v, Math.sin(a) * r);\n        p.addScaledVector(path.normal, Math.sin(a * 3 + ri) * .055); p.y -= .15;\n        dummy.position.copy(p); dummy.scale.setScalar(d.scale); dummy.updateMatrix();\n        particles.setMatrixAt(i, dummy.matrix);\n      });\n      particles.instanceMatrix.needsUpdate = true;\n      placeInstances(copperParticles, copperAnchors, 1, .4, -time * .65);\n      renderer.render(scene, camera);\n    }\n    // Compose a complete first frame even when reduced motion starts paused.\n    rings.forEach((r, i) => paths[i].normal.set(0, 0, 1).applyEuler(r.group.rotation));\n    anchors.forEach((d, i) => {\n      const path = paths[i % 3], a = d.a, r = path.radius + d.lane;\n      p.copy(path.u).multiplyScalar(Math.cos(a) * r).addScaledVector(path.v, Math.sin(a) * r); p.y -= .15;\n      dummy.position.copy(p); dummy.scale.setScalar(d.scale); dummy.updateMatrix(); particles.setMatrixAt(i, dummy.matrix);\n    });\n    placeInstances(copperParticles, copperAnchors, 1, .4, 0);\n    renderer.render(scene, camera);\n    requestAnimationFrame(frame);\n  })();\n  </script>\n</body>\n</html>",
